WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:02.535
is going to meet with the Polish

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.303
president, Duda, here in Warsaw.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:05.438
They're going to talk about

00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:06.773
support for Ukraine, bolstering

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:07.707
nato obviously.

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.041
Poland has greatly felt the

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:10.543
impact of Russia's invasion.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.011
Their defense forces have grown

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.679
in numbers as well since Russia

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.649
started invading its neighbor,

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:17.383
and when we got here in Warsaw,

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.719
we spoke with some of the newest

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.588
Polish recruits about why

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:23.489
they're signing up for Poland's

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.894
version of the National Guard.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:29.095
Some of them have never held a

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:32.965
gun in their life.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:36.002
They are teachers, farmers,

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:37.537
bankers, and even an aspiring

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.205
opera singer, now volunteering

00:00:39.338 --> 00:00:42.942
for basic training in Warsaw.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:46.078
They are days away from

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:51.250
graduating and becoming infantry

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:52.585
personnel, the Polish version of

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.386
the U.S. National Guard.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:58.591
When Russia invaded Ukraine, and

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:02.595
placed war on Poland's doorstep,

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:03.796
they saw rise in recruits.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.265
Now the defense minister expects

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:07.667
recruits to reach 50,000 in the

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:08.601
coming years.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.102
&gt;&gt; Awareness is the first step

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.605
of this.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.040
&gt;&gt; Reporter: For Poland, the

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:15.408
country with the lowest gun

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.476
ownership per capita in Europe,

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.078
the invasion became a national

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:22.048
call to arms for people with day

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:22.615
jobs.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.116
&gt;&gt; We slowly turned civilians

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.551
into soldiers.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.186
We teach them the structures.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.288
We teach them how to wear the

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:29.622
uniform.

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:31.324
We teach them how to behave.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.125
We teach them when to salute,

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.627
when to not salute.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:35.828
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Mary, a 36-year-old

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.964
mother of two, now finds herself

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.999
balancing life as a banker on

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.701
the battlefield.

00:01:41.834 --> 00:01:43.436
&gt;&gt; I'm very happy that I have

00:01:43.569 --> 00:01:46.639
this possibility to work and to

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:46.906
be a soldier.

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.174
&gt;&gt; Reporter: 22-year-old Laura

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.643
is an aspiring opera singer who

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.645
joined the tdf in solidarity

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:53.980
after being shocked by Russia's

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.748
brutal invasion.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.817
&gt;&gt; Young people, we are shocked

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.652
about the situation, and we want

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:04.056
to help the Ukraine.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:04.790
&gt;&gt; Reporter: And have you ever

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.358
handled a gun before?

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.793
&gt;&gt; No.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:08.060
No.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:11.797
When I came here, it was my

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:15.668
first -- first connect with

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:16.669
everything military.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.136
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Did it surprise

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:17.403
you?

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.672
&gt;&gt; A little bit, yes, because

00:02:19.805 --> 00:02:20.673
it's heavy.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.507
&gt;&gt; Very heavy.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.977
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Laura's twin sister

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:25.711
joined the tdf before her, and

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.314
their mom has also just applied.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.749
&gt;&gt; Your mom is joining tdf?

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:31.284
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.353
&gt;&gt; And you're in fdf and your

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:34.820
sister?

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:35.955
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Laura, Mary, and

00:02:36.088 --> 00:02:38.724
the rest of the recruits undergo

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:41.060
16 days of basic training,

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.295
graduating, and then reporting

00:02:42.695 --> 00:02:42.962
once a month.

00:02:43.095 --> 00:02:45.331
&gt;&gt; In tdf, you have to learn how

00:02:45.464 --> 00:02:49.168
to crawl before you walk.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.470
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Putin's unprovoked

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:56.075
war in Ukraine prompting civil

00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:59.745
readiness not seen in Europe in

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:00.112
decades.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.147
&gt;&gt; You're seeing them turn into

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:05.952
amazing soldiers.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:06.719
&gt;&gt; Reporter: Despite their

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:07.053
differences.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:10.756
&gt;&gt;&gt; One thing unites the

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:13.592
territorial area.

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:14.860
&gt;&gt; Everyone you see behind you

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.263
loves their country, and

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.732
regardless of their social

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:22.935
economic status, education

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:23.669
level, employment, they all love

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.739
Poland, and they all want to

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.942
serve with a flag on their

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:30.309
shoulder.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:31.010
Patriotism is the common

00:03:31.143 --> 00:03:35.681
denominator.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.184
&gt;&gt; Patriotism is the common

00:03:38.317 --> 00:03:38.751
denominator.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.752
&gt;&gt; Reporter: It was just amazing

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.721
to spend several hours with

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:42.021
them.

00:03:42.154 --> 00:03:45.124
&gt;&gt; That was a great piece.

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:45.791
Like, really, really great.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:46.425
&gt;&gt; Reporter: It was great.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.462
I think it's something we never

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:50.262
expected to see, and all of

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.864
these people giving so much for

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.733
the cause from all walks of

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:57.470
life, it was fascinating.

00:03:57.603 --> 00:03:57.970
&gt;&gt; All right.

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.071
&gt;&gt; Reporter: You guys know when

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:01.807
a story like this, it takes a

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:02.775
team effort.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.443
Betty and clay and Antonio, we

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:05.911
were all out there setting this

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:06.178
up.

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:07.480
It was amazing to see these

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:10.316
everyday, regular people who now

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:11.250
have never held a gun in their

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:12.952
lives and they're signing up to

